          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most houses, the Westinghouse WGen7500c is the 9,500 watt generator to buy: full 30-amp running output, remote start and a CO sensor, without paying for fuel systems you will not use. If you want propane, the Champion 201277 does the same job on two fuels for a fair price.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Pay for an inverter when noise or a fussy furnace board matters, and pay for the tri fuel DuroMax when you have a gas line and never want to store fuel again. Whatever you buy, pair it with a 30-amp inlet and transfer switch, and size your loads on the running watts, not the number on the box.
          </p>
